---
import Base from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  lang="en"
  title="Products · ORDO"
  description="ORDO product system: instruments (hardware) and software organized by verifiable facts, boundaries, and re-entry across interruptions."
  keywords={["ORDO", "products", "instruments", "hardware", "software", "RESPECTA", "re-entry"]}
>
  <section class="page">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="hero" aria-label="Product system">
        <h1 class="h1">Product system</h1>
        <p class="lead">Organized by rule capability: boundary facts / responsibility facts / traceable facts.</p>
        <p class="note">
          ORDO instruments are not reminder systems, and they do not make decisions for you. They turn key rules into
          <strong>checkable facts</strong>, so after interruptions and handoffs you can return to the same position of judgment.
        </p>

        <div class="hero-actions" aria-label="Related">
          <a class="btn" href="/en/shop">Hardware store</a>
          <a class="btn" href="/en/software">Software</a>
          <a class="btn" href="/en/manufacturing">Manufacturing &amp; verification</a>
          <a class="btn ghost" href="/en/releases">Releases</a>
        </div>
        <p class="jump">
          Quick links:
          <a class="inline" href="#tiers">System tiers</a> ·
          <a class="inline" href="#families">Product families</a> ·
          <a class="inline" href="#redlines">Paradigm redlines</a>
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      <section class="section" id="tiers" aria-label="System tiers">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2 class="h2">System tiers</h2>
          <p class="sublead">Tiered by “rule capability”, not by feature stacking.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="grid-4" role="list" aria-label="System tiers">
          <article class="card tier" role="listitem">
            <div class="no" aria-hidden="true">01</div>
            <div class="tier-head">
              <div class="tier-cn">Facts layer</div>
              <div class="tier-en">Facts</div>
            </div>
            <p class="p">Expose key states as facts: visible, returnable, checkable.</p>
          </article>

          <article class="card tier" role="listitem">
            <div class="no" aria-hidden="true">02</div>
            <div class="tier-head">
              <div class="tier-cn">Scenes layer</div>
              <div class="tier-en">Scenes</div>
            </div>
            <p class="p">Package facts into deployable scenes: reading, work, handoff, reproduction—without changing judgment.</p>
          </article>

          <article class="card tier" role="listitem">
            <div class="no" aria-hidden="true">03</div>
            <div class="tier-head">
              <div class="tier-cn">Orgs layer</div>
              <div class="tier-en">Orgs</div>
            </div>
            <p class="p">Stabilize scenes into a shared language: consistent boundaries and responsibility facts across people.</p>
          </article>

          <article class="card tier" role="listitem">
            <div class="no" aria-hidden="true">04</div>
            <div class="tier-head">
              <div class="tier-cn">Standards layer</div>
              <div class="tier-en">Standards</div>
            </div>
            <p class="p">Standards are for reading and checking; they are not automatic endorsements of any product.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      <section class="section" id="families" aria-label="Product families">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2 class="h2">Product families</h2>
          <p class="sublead">Three typical scenes organized by checkable facts.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="grid-3" role="list" aria-label="Product families">
          <article class="card" role="listitem">
            <div class="card-head">
              <div class="k">Boundary facts system</div>
              <div class="mini">Stop point / next action / handed off</div>
            </div>
            <p class="p">Turn “stop point / next action / handed off” into anchors—so you can return to the same position of judgment.</p>
            <div class="tags" aria-label="Use cases">
              <span class="tag">Reading</span><span class="tag">Writing</span><span class="tag">Communication</span><span class="tag">Handoffs</span>
            </div>
            <ul class="list">
              <li>Return fast after interruption</li>
              <li>Switch tasks without rebuilding context</li>
            </ul>
          </article>

          <article class="card" role="listitem">
            <div class="card-head">
              <div class="k">Responsibility facts system</div>
              <div class="mini">Fulfilled / handed off / closed</div>
            </div>
            <p class="p">Make “fulfilled / handed off / closed” into facts—without reminders or blame.</p>
            <div class="tags" aria-label="Use cases">
              <span class="tag">Home duties</span><span class="tag">Care items</span><span class="tag">Maintenance</span><span class="tag">Team handoff</span>
            </div>
            <ul class="list">
              <li>Put responsibilities in reality, not verbal promises</li>
              <li>Clarify who did what, when, and how to verify</li>
            </ul>
          </article>

          <article class="card" role="listitem">
            <div class="card-head">
              <div class="k">Traceable facts system</div>
              <div class="mini">Last happened / last confirmed / reproduction basis</div>
            </div>
            <p class="p">Anchor “last happened / last confirmed / reproduction basis” as facts.</p>
            <div class="tags" aria-label="Use cases">
              <span class="tag">Creation</span><span class="tag">Pro work</span><span class="tag">Review</span><span class="tag">Reproduction</span>
            </div>
            <ul class="list">
              <li>Keep key evidence in the real world, easy to return to</li>
              <li>Reproduce decision background across time without memory reliance</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      <section class="section" id="redlines" aria-label="Paradigm redlines">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2 class="h2">Paradigm redlines</h2>
          <p class="sublead">No monitoring, no scoring, no punishment, no forced reminders.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="quote" role="note">
          <p>
            ORDO products do not rely on monitoring, scoring, punishment, or forced reminders. Instruments do not drive your
            decisions—only provide a stable reference when you ask.
          </p>
          <p class="quote-foot">Silent when you are away; accurate when you return.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    /* Align with Manufacturing page layout */

    .hero{ padding-top: 10px; max-width: 104ch; }

    .lead{ margin: 12px 0 0; color: rgba(220,235,240,.78); line-height: 1.85; max-width: 92ch; }

    .hero-actions{ margin-top: 14px; display:flex; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
.note{ margin: 12px 0 0; color: rgba(220,235,240,.60); font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.75; max-width: 104ch; }
    .jump{ margin: 10px 0 0; color: rgba(220,235,240,.56); font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.75; }
    .inline{ color: rgba(240,252,255,0.92); text-underline-offset: 2px; }

    .section{ margin-top: 14px; }
    .section-head{ display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:flex-end; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; }

    .sublead{ margin: 6px 0 0; color: rgba(220,235,240,0.66); line-height: 1.75; max-width: 110ch; }

    .card-head{ display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:flex-end; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .k{ font-weight: 800; color: rgba(240,252,255,0.92); letter-spacing: 0.08em; font-size: 12px; }
    .mini{ margin-top: 6px; font-size: 12px; color: rgba(220,235,240,.60); }
    .p{ margin: 10px 0 0; color: rgba(220,235,240,.74); line-height: 1.85; }

    /* Desktop layout: 2 columns per row */
    .grid-3{ display:grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0,1fr)); gap: 12px; margin-top: 12px; }
    .grid-3 > article:nth-child(3){ grid-column: 1 / -1; max-width: 560px; justify-self: center; }

    .grid-4{ display:grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0,1fr)); gap: 12px; margin-top: 12px; }

    .tier .no{
      position:absolute;
      top: 12px;
      right: 14px;
      font-size: 12px;
      color: rgba(220,235,240,0.24);
      letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    }
    .tier-head{ display:flex; gap: 10px; align-items: baseline; margin-top: 2px; }
    .tier-cn{ font-weight: 780; color: rgba(240,252,255,0.92); }
    .tier-en{ font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: 0.12em; color: rgba(220,235,240,0.52); }

    .tags{ margin-top: 10px; display:flex; gap: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .tag{
      padding: 5px 10px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      border: 1px solid rgba(220,235,240,0.10);
      background: rgba(10,22,26,0.10);
      color: rgba(220,235,240,0.70);
      font-size: 12px;
    }

    .list{ margin: 12px 0 0; padding-left: 18px; color: rgba(220,235,240,.70); line-height: 1.75; }
    .list li{ margin: 6px 0; }

    .quote{
      margin-top: 12px;
      border-radius: 18px;
      border: 1px solid rgba(220,235,240,0.10);
      background: rgba(10,22,26,0.10);
      box-shadow: 0 10px 34px rgba(0,0,0,0.30), inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.06);
      padding: 16px;
      color: rgba(220,235,240,0.80);
      line-height: 1.9;
    }
    .quote p{ margin: 0; }
    .quote p + p{ margin-top: 10px; }
    .quote-foot{ color: rgba(240,252,255,0.90); }

    @media (max-width: 1100px){
      .grid-4{ grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0,1fr)); }
      .grid-3{ grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0,1fr)); }
    }
    @media (max-width: 780px){
      .grid-3{ grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    }
    @media (max-width: 680px){

      .grid-4{ grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    }
  </style>
</Base>
